---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# Gives the filter that OPENS a fused run the throwaway copy its predicate eats.
# 281/282/283 splice a Φ.hone.dup in front of a filter that follows another
# pragma they recognise (a map, a peek, another filter, a stateful guard); a
# filter with nothing fusable in front of it — first in the method, or behind a
# Φ.hone.box or a mapMulti pragma, neither of which is a distill — has no
# predecessor to splice behind, so 401 hands 4xx a distill whose `start` is still
# "filter" and whose body opens with the predicate call. This rule prepends the
# missing dup and flips `start` to "dup" so it fires once per run.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: 413 runs AFTER 411, which may still unwind a box/distill/unbox
# sandwich back to a primitive distill and move `accepted` off the wrapper, and
# BEFORE 421, which prepends the head `Wrapper.xValue()` when the distill
# receives a wrapper while its first operator accepts the primitive — and which
# overwrites `accepted` with the wrapper `bridge-input` on the way. Going in
# first means 421's unbox lands in FRONT of the guard, so the run unboxes once
# and the guard copies the primitive the predicate is about to consume; its width
# comes from the pre-421 `accepted`, which still names that primitive.
#
# Running after 421 instead — where this rule sat, as 431, until #811 — read the
# overwritten wrapper `accepted` and emitted a one-slot `dup` of the wrapper, so
# every stage behind the guard found a java/lang/Long where it needed a `long`. A
# lone boxed filter happened to survive that (#704: nothing came after the
# guard), but a second filter's two-slot `dup2` popped that single one-slot
# reference and the class died at load with "Operand stack underflow".
name: dup-before-filter-distill
pattern: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.distill,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    bridge-input ↦ 𝑒-bridge-input,
    bridge-output ↦ 𝑒-bridge-output,
    start ↦ "filter",
    accepted ↦ 𝑒-accepted,
    returned ↦ 𝑒-returned,
    static ↦ 𝑒-static,
    state ↦ 𝑒-state,
    body ↦ ⟦ 𝐵-body, ρ ↦ ∅ ⟧
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    φ ↦ Φ.hone.distill,
    class ↦ 𝑒-class,
    bridge-input ↦ 𝑒-bridge-input,
    bridge-output ↦ 𝑒-bridge-output,
    start ↦ "dup",
    accepted ↦ 𝑒-accepted,
    returned ↦ 𝑒-returned,
    static ↦ 𝑒-static,
    state ↦ 𝑒-state,
    body ↦ ⟦
      i-dup ↦ ⟦ φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.𝜏-dup ⟧,
      𝐵-body,
      ρ ↦ ∅
    ⟧
  ⟧
where:
  - meta: 𝑒-dup
    function: sed
    args:
      - 𝑒-accepted
      - '"s/^[DJ]$/dup2/g"'
      - '"s/^(B|C|F|I|S|Z|L.+;)$/dup/g"'
  - meta: 𝜏-dup
    function: tau
    args: [𝑒-dup]
